{"G1029":{"id":"G1029","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1029","disambiguated_id":"G1029 =","unique_id":"G1029","headword":"βρόχος","transliteration":"brochos","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"restraint","definition_en":"βρόχος, -ου, ὁ, \n [in LXX: Pro.6:5 (יָד) 7:21 (חֵלֶק) 22:25 (מוֹקֵשׁ), 3Ma.4:8 * ;] \na noose, a slip-knot, a halter: metaphorically, a restraint (not, as AV, R, txt., a snare): 1Co.7:35.†\n (AS)","source_line":1151}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"enlaçar","count":1}]},"G138":{"id":"G138","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0138","disambiguated_id":"G0138 =","unique_id":"G0138","headword":"αἱρέω","transliteration":"ahireō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to choose","definition_en":"αἱρέω, \n [in LXX for אמר hi., בּחר, etc. ;] \nto take; Mid., -ομαι (M, Pr., 158 f.; MM, VGT, see word), to choose: Php.1:22, 2Th.2:13, Heb.11:25. (Cf. ἀν-, ἀφ-, δι-, ἐξ-, καθ-, περι-, προ-αιρέω.) †\n (AS)","source_line":236}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"sei","count":1},{"gloss":"escolheu","count":1},{"gloss":"preferiu","count":1}]},"G145":{"id":"G145","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0145","disambiguated_id":"G0145 =","unique_id":"G0145","headword":"αἰσθητήριον","transliteration":"aisthētērion","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"sense","definition_en":"αἰσθητήριον, -ου, τό \n (αἰσθάνομαι), [in LXX: Jer.4:19 (קִיר), 4Ma.2:22 * ;] \nsense, organ of perception: Heb.5:14 (MM, VGT, see word).†\n (AS)","source_line":243}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"sentidos","count":1}]},"G1496":{"id":"G1496","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1496","disambiguated_id":"G1496 =","unique_id":"G1496","headword":"εἰδωλολάτρης","transliteration":"eidōlolatrēs","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"idolater","definition_en":"εἰδωλολάτρης, -ου, ὁ \n (εἴδωλου + λάτρις, a hireling), \nan idolator: 1Co.5:10, 11 6:9 10:7 Eph.5:5 Rev.21:8 22:15 (Cremer, 709).†\n (AS)","source_line":1636}],"occurrence_count":7,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"idólatras","count":5},{"gloss":"idólatra","count":2}]},"G1569":{"id":"G1569","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1569","disambiguated_id":"G1569 =","unique_id":"G1569","headword":"ἔκθαμβος","transliteration":"ekthambos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"astonished","definition_en":"ἔκ-θαμβος, -ον\n (θάμβος), [in LXX: Wis.10:19, Da TH Dan.7:7 (dreadful, terrible: אֵמְתָּנִי) * ;] \namazed (cf. Polyb., xx, 10, 9): Act.3:11.†\n (AS)","source_line":1709}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"totalmente-atônito","count":1}]},"G1677":{"id":"G1677","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1677","disambiguated_id":"G1677 =","unique_id":"G1677","headword":"ἐλλογέω","transliteration":"ellogeō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to charge","definition_en":"ἐλλογάω, -ῶ\n (a κοινή word, elsewhere usually -έω; cf. Bl., § 22, 2), \nto charge to one's account, impute: Phm 18 (on parallels, cf. Deiss., LAE, 79 f., 335 f.; Milligan, NTD, 73; MM, Exp., xii); of sin, Rom.5:13 (Cremer, 400).†\n (AS)","source_line":1818}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"considerado","count":1},{"gloss":"conta","count":1}]},"G1720":{"id":"G1720","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1720","disambiguated_id":"G1720 =","unique_id":"G1720","headword":"ἐμφυσάω","transliteration":"emphusaō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to breathe into","definition_en":"ἐμ-φυσάω, -ῶ\n (φυσάω, to blow), [in LXX for נָפַח, etc. ;] \nto breathe into (cf. Gen.2:7, Wis.15:11, a1.), breathe upon: Jhn.20:22.†\n (AS)","source_line":1861}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"soprou","count":1}]},"G2620":{"id":"G2620","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2620","disambiguated_id":"G2620 =","unique_id":"G2620","headword":"κατακαυχάομαι","transliteration":"katakauchaomai","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to boast","definition_en":"κατα-καυχάομαι, -ῶμαι \n [in LXX: Zec.10:12 (הָלַךְ hith.), Jer.50:11 (עָלַז), Jer.50:38 (הָלַל)* ;] \n__1. to boast against, exult over: with genitive, Rom.11:18, Jas.2:13; before κατά, with genitive, Jas.3:14 (T, om. κατά). \n __2. before ἐν, to glory in (Za., l.with, Jer.27:38).†\n (AS)","source_line":2811}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"orgulhes","count":1},{"gloss":"orgulhares","count":1},{"gloss":"triunfa-sobre","count":1},{"gloss":"orgulheis","count":1}]},"G2688":{"id":"G2688","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2688","disambiguated_id":"G2688 =","unique_id":"G2688","headword":"κατάστημα","transliteration":"katastēma","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"behavior","definition_en":"κατά-στημα, -τος, τό\n (καθίστημι), in LXX: 3Ma.5:45 (-εμα, A) * ;] \n__1. condition, of health, etc. \n __2. demeanour: Tit.2:3 (for exx. see Field, Notes, 220).†\n (AS)","source_line":2879}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"bons","count":1}]},"G2984":{"id":"G2984","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2984","disambiguated_id":"G2984 = the Greek of","unique_id":"H3929H","headword":"Λάμεχ","transliteration":"Lamech","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Lamech","definition_en":"Λάμεχ, ὁ indecl. (Heb. לֶמֶךְ), \n Lamech (Gen.5:25): Luk.3:36.† \n (AS)","source_line":3182}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Lameque","count":1}]},"G3027":{"id":"G3027","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3027","disambiguated_id":"G3027 =","unique_id":"G3027","headword":"λῃστής","transliteration":"lēstēs","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"robber/rebel","definition_en":"λῃστής, -οῦ, ὁ\n (Ep. ληίς = λεία, booty), [in LXX for גְּדוּד, etc. ;] \na robber, brigand: Mat.21:13 (LXX) Mat.26:55 27:38, 44, Mrk.11:17 14:48 15:27, Luk.10:30, 36 19:46 22:52, Jhn.10:1, 8 18:40, 2Co.11:26.†\n SYN.: κλέπτης, q.v (AS)","source_line":3229}],"occurrence_count":15,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"ladrões","count":5},{"gloss":"ladrão","count":3},{"gloss":"assaltantes","count":3},{"gloss":"criminosos","count":1},{"gloss":"um-bandido","count":1},{"gloss":"assaltante","count":1},{"gloss":"de-assaltantes","count":1}]},"G3667":{"id":"G3667","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3667","disambiguated_id":"G3667 =","unique_id":"G3667","headword":"ὁμοίωμα","transliteration":"homoiōma","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"likeness","definition_en":"ὁμοίωμα, -τος, τό\n (ὁμοιόω), [in LXX for דְּמוּת, תַּבְנִית, תְּמוּנָה, etc. ;] \nthat which is made like something; \n __(a) concrete, an image, like­ness (Psa.106:20, Eze.1:5, 1Ma.3:48, al.) : Rev.9:7; \n __(b) abstract, like­ness, resemblance: Rom.5:14 6:5 8:3, Php.2:7; ἐν ὁ. εἰκόνος, Rom.1:23.†\n SYN.: εἰκών (which see), ὁμοίωσις (AS)","source_line":3783}],"occurrence_count":6,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"semelhança","count":5},{"gloss":"aparência","count":1}]},"G368":{"id":"G368","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0368","disambiguated_id":"G0368 =","unique_id":"G0368","headword":"ἀναντίρρητος","transliteration":"anantirrētos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"indisputable","definition_en":"ἀν-αντί-ρητος\n (Τ, -ρρητος, -ον (ῥητός, spoken), [in Sm.: Job.11:2 33:13 * ;] \nnot to be contradicted, undeniable: Act.19:36 (MM, VGT, see word).†\n (AS)","source_line":474}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"incontestáveis","count":1}]},"G3722":{"id":"G3722","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3722","disambiguated_id":"G3722 =","unique_id":"G3722","headword":"ὄρθρος","transliteration":"orthros","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"dawn","definition_en":"ὄρθρος, -ου, ὁ \n [in LXX for שַׁחַר, בֹּקֶר, etc. ;] \ndaybreak, dawn: ὄρθρου βαθέως (M, Pr., 73), at early dawn, Luk.24:1; ὄρθρου, Jhn.8:2; ὑπὸ τὸν ὄ., Act.5:21 (cf. MM, xviii).†\n (AS)","source_line":3839}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"cedo","count":2}]},"G3870":{"id":"G3870","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3870","disambiguated_id":"G3870 =","unique_id":"G3870","headword":"παρακαλέω","transliteration":"parakaleō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to plead/comfort","definition_en":"παρακαλέω, -ῶ, \n [in LXX chiefly for נחם ni., pi. ;] \n __1. to call to one, call for, summon: Act.28:20 (R, mg.; R, txt., entreat); hence (of the gods: Dem., Xen., al.), to invoke, call on, beseech, entreat: τ. πατέρα μου, Mat.26:53; τ. κύριον, 2Co.12:8; in late writers (Polyb., Diod., al.; rarely in LXX; in π., see Deiss., LAE, 176.14), also of men: absol., Phm 9; with accusative, Mat.8:5, Mrk.1:40, Act.16:9, al.; with inf., Mrk.5:17, Luk.8:41, Act.8:31, al.; before ἵνα (see M, Pr., 205, 208), Mt 14\"36, Mrk.5:18, Luk.8:31, al. \n __2. to admonish, exhort: absol., Luk.3:18, Rom.12:8, 2Ti.4:2, al.; with accusative, Act.15:32, 1Th.2:11, Heb.3:13, al.; id. before inf., Act.11:23, Rom.12:1, Php.4:2, 1Th.4:10, al.; before ἵνα (see M, Pr., l.with), 1Co.1:10, 2Co.8:6, 1Th.4:1, al. \n __3. to cheer, encourage, comfort (Plut., LXX: Jb 43, Isa.35:3, Sir.43:24, al.): with accusative, 2Co.1:6, Eph.6:22, Col.2:2, al.; id. before ἐν, 1Th.4:18; διά, 2Co.1:4; pass., Mat.5:4, Luk.16:25, Act.20:12. \n SYN.: παραμυθέω (cf. M, Th., 25). (AS)","source_line":3988}],"occurrence_count":109,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"rogo","count":13},{"gloss":"rogaram","count":9},{"gloss":"rogando","count":6},{"gloss":"exortando","count":5},{"gloss":"exorta","count":5},{"gloss":"exortamos","count":4},{"gloss":"roguei","count":4},{"gloss":"peço","count":4},{"gloss":"consolados","count":3},{"gloss":"rogavam","count":3},{"gloss":"rogou","count":3},{"gloss":"eu","count":3},{"gloss":"exortar","count":3},{"gloss":"rogava","count":2},{"gloss":"consolado","count":2},{"gloss":"exortava","count":2},{"gloss":"rogamos","count":2},{"gloss":"consola","count":2},{"gloss":"consolar","count":2},{"gloss":"somos-consolados","count":2},{"gloss":"consolai","count":2},{"gloss":"console","count":2},{"gloss":"consolada","count":1},{"gloss":"suplicou","count":1},{"gloss":"suplicaste","count":1},{"gloss":"orar","count":1},{"gloss":"rogar","count":1},{"gloss":"implorava","count":1},{"gloss":"rogam","count":1},{"gloss":"e-rogou","count":1}]},"G4267":{"id":"G4267","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4267","disambiguated_id":"G4267 =","unique_id":"G4267","headword":"προγινώσκω","transliteration":"proginōskō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to know/choose","definition_en":"προ-γινώσκω \n [in LXX: Wis.6:13 8:8 18:6 * ;] \nto know beforehand, foreknow: 2Pe.3:17; with accusative of person(s), Act.26:5; of the Divine foreknowledge, Rom.8:29 11:2, 1Pe.1:20.†\n (AS)","source_line":4397}],"occurrence_count":5,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"conhecendo-de-antemão","count":1},{"gloss":"desde-antes-conheceu","count":1},{"gloss":"desde-antes-conhecia","count":1},{"gloss":"conhecido-desde","count":1},{"gloss":"sabendo","count":1}]},"G4457":{"id":"G4457","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4457","disambiguated_id":"G4457 =","unique_id":"G4457","headword":"πώρωσις","transliteration":"pōrōsis","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"hardening","definition_en":"πώρωσις, -εως, ἡ\n (πωρόω), \na covering with a callus, a hardening: metaphorically, Mrk.3:6, Rom.11:2, Eph.4:18.†\n (AS)","source_line":4590}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"dureza","count":2},{"gloss":"endurecimento","count":1}]},"G4588":{"id":"G4588","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4588","disambiguated_id":"G4588 =","unique_id":"G4588","headword":"Σέργιος","transliteration":"Sergios","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Sergius","definition_en":"Σέργιος, -ου, ὁ \n Sergius, surnamed Paulus: Act.13:7.†\n (AS)","source_line":4726}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Sérgio","count":1}]},"G4789":{"id":"G4789","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4789","disambiguated_id":"G4789 =","unique_id":"G4789","headword":"συγκληρονόμος","transliteration":"sugklēronomos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"co-heir","definition_en":"συν-κληρο-νόμος (Rec. συγκ-), -ου, ὁ \n a co-inheritor, fellow-heir: Rom.8:17, Eph.3:6; with genitive of thing(s), Heb.11:9, 1Pe.3:7 (for exx., see Deiss., LAE, 88 f.).†\n (AS)","source_line":4937}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"herdeiros","count":3},{"gloss":"coerdeiros","count":1}]},"G4843":{"id":"G4843","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4843","disambiguated_id":"G4843 =","unique_id":"G4843","headword":"συμπεριλαμβάνω","transliteration":"sumperilambanō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to embrace","definition_en":"συν-περι-λαμβάνω (Rec. συμπ-), \n __1. to enclose (Eze.5:3 (צוּר) *). \n __2. to embrace: with accusative of person(s), Act.20:10.†\n (AS)","source_line":4995}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"abraçando","count":1}]},"G5018":{"id":"G5018","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5018","disambiguated_id":"G5018 = a Group member of","unique_id":"G5019","headword":"Ταρσεύς","transliteration":"Tarseus","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-L","gloss_en":"of Tarsus","definition_en":"Ταρσεύς, -έως, ὁ\n (Ταρσός), \nof Tarsus: Act.9:11 21:39.†\n (AS)","source_line":5170}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"tarsense","count":1},{"gloss":"Tarso","count":1}]},"G5043":{"id":"G5043","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5043","disambiguated_id":"G5043 =","unique_id":"G5043","headword":"τέκνον","transliteration":"teknon","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"child","definition_en":"τέκνον, -ου, τό \n (τίκτω), [in LXX chiefly for בֵּן, also for יֶלֶד, etc. ;] \nthat which is begotten, born (cf. Scottish bairn), a child of either sex: Mrk.13:12, Luk.1:7, Act.7:5; pl., Mat.7:11, Mrk.7:27, Luk.1:17, Eph.6:1, al.; τέκνα ἐπαγγελίας, Rom.9:8; τ. τῆς σαρκός, ib.; in a wider sense (as Heb. בָּנִים), of posterity, Mat.2:18, Luk.3:8, al.; specif., of a male child, Mat.21:28, Act.21:21, a,l.; in voc. as a form of kindly address from an elder to a junior or from a teacher to a disciple, Mat.9:2 21:28, Mrk.2:5, Luk.2:48; τ. μου (= cl. τ. μοι; see Bl., §37, 5), Gal.4:19 (τεκνία, WH, txt.), 2Ti.2:1. Metaphorical, \n__(a) of disciples (apart from direct address, see supr.): Phm 10, 1Ti.1:2, Tit.1:4, 3Jo.4; \n __(b) with reference to the Fatherhood of God (see: πατήρ, γεννάω), τέκνα τ. θεοῦ (cf. Isa.30:1, Wis.16:21): Rom.8:16, Eph.5:1, Php.2:15; and esp. in Johannine bks. (cf. Westc, Epp. Jo., 94, 120), Jhn.1:12, 1Jn.3:1 al.; \n __(with) of those who imitate others and are therefore regarded as the spiritual offspring of their exemplars: Mat.3:9, Luk.3:8, Jhn.8:39, Rom.9:7, 1Pe.3:6; τ. διαβόλου, 1Jn.3:10; \n __(d) as in Heb. (LXX, Jol.2:23, Psa.149:2, 1Ma.1:38), of the inhabitants of a city: Mat.23:37, Luk.13:34 19:44, Gal.4:25; \n __(e) with an adjectival genitive, frequently rendering a Heb. expression, adopted from LXX or formed on the analogy of its language, but sometimes with parallels in Gk. writers (see Deiss., BS, 161ff.): τέκνα φωτός, Eph.5:8; τ. ὑπακοῆς, 1Pe.1:14; κατάρας, 2Pe.2:14; ὀργῆς, Eph.2:3. \n SYN.: see: παῖς. (AS)","source_line":5195}],"occurrence_count":99,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"filhos","count":75},{"gloss":"filho","count":16},{"gloss":"Filho","count":5},{"gloss":"advertir","count":1},{"gloss":"filhinhos","count":1},{"gloss":"filhas","count":1}]},"G5152":{"id":"G5152","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5152","disambiguated_id":"G5152 =","unique_id":"G5152","headword":"τρίστεγος","transliteration":"tristegos","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"third story","definition_en":"τρίστεγος, -ον (τρεῖς, στέγη) \n [in Sm.: Gen.6:17(16), Eze.42:6 * ;] \nof three stories: τὸ τ. (sc. ὄκημα), \n the third story, Act.20:9 (Dion., FlJ, al.).†\n (AS)","source_line":5307}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"terceiro-andar","count":1}]},"G819":{"id":